# What belongs in this repository is the DESIGN and the tools that build it.
# Everything a tool regenerates from those stays out: the synthesis and
# simulation trees alone come to about 200 MB, and a tracked build product is
# worse than no build product, because it can silently disagree with the
# sources sitting next to it.
#
# Tracked, deliberately: the VHDL, the assembler and its programs, the
# testbenches and checkers, the constraint file, the Diamond project scripts,
# and the documentation.

# ---- GHDL -----------------------------------------------------------------
sim/work/
*.cf
*.o
*.vcd

# ---- Lattice Diamond ------------------------------------------------------
# Every build product is regenerated by syn/build_vendor.py; only that script,
# the Synplify project, the .lpf and the .xcf are tracked.
syn/work_pharvard/
syn/vendor/
syn/estimate/
syn/dtest/
syn/lcd_test/

*.jed
*.bit
*.mrp
*.twr
*.par
*.ncd
*.ngd
*.ngo
*.edi
*.edn
*.srp
*.srf
*.srr
*.bgn
*.pad
*.prf
*.rpt
*.mti
*.cr.mti
*.ldf
*.sty
*.pty

# ---- tool chatter ---------------------------------------------------------
stdout.log*
stdout_job.log*
synlog.tcl
*.log

# ---- editors / OS ---------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.vscode/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
sim/work_jitter/
sim/work_slots/
